      "writtenOn": "2026-05-04T21:33:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a great idea, thanks.\n\nO why must java prevent us from having static methods on non static classes? This forces us to break encapsulation. :( It\u0027s not like static classes are any different from public file level classes (i.e. they aren\u0027t really static!).",
      "parentUuid": "f0e0f599_d187ea77",
      "revId": "0e8488001e4f476f998b012358576fae90ec8141",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
